     1	# Test-harness audit-log isolation (dogfood doctrine)
     2	
     3	> **Status:** shipped in PLAN-119 (S182). Durable fix for the lesson
     4	> *"verification in the live env pollutes the audit chain"*.
     5	
     6	## The problem
     7	
     8	This repo **dogfoods an audit-emitting framework in its own repo, against the
     9	real `~/.claude`**. Every hook that runs, and every audit event that is emitted,
    10	resolves its audit-log path from the ambient environment. When a test, a probe,
    11	or an ad-hoc `pytest`/hook invocation runs without an isolated environment, it
    12	writes **real-looking audit events into the LIVE
    13	`~/.claude/projects/ceo-orchestration/audit-log.jsonl`**. Those events carry
    14	HMACs computed under test conditions (or against a different chain head, or by a
    15	stale producer), so they do **not** verify against the live chain:
    16	`audit-verify-chain` later reads `tamper` and `audit-log.errors` floods.
    17	
    18	S181 forensics: of 1738 live-log lines, ~1690 were test/probe pollution; only
    19	~47 were the real session.
    20	
    21	## The two axes of the fix (PLAN-119)
    22	
    23	The naive idea — a kernel guard that refuses to write "when this looks like a
    24	test" — is an **audit-suppression vector** (an attacker could divert a real
    25	session's events off the live chain) and was rejected (WS-B-DROPPED). The robust
    26	design works on two axes an attacker cannot use to silence a real session:
    27	
    28	### Axis 1 — destination redirect (WS-A / WS-C)
    29	
    30	A **session-scoped autouse pytest fixture** (`_lib/test_isolation.py`,
    31	registered by the root + `.claude/hooks/tests/` + `.claude/scripts/tests/`
    32	conftests) redirects the **full audit/HMAC env carrier set** to a per-session
    33	tmpdir *before any test body runs*:
    34	
    35	- **SET** (to the tmp tree): `CEO_AUDIT_LOG_DIR`, `CEO_PROJECT_STATE_DIR`, and
    36	  `CEO_TEST_HARNESS=1`. `CEO_AUDIT_LOG_DIR` is the PRIMARY resolver for every
    37	  audit path (`audit_emit._audit_dir` / `audit_hmac._audit_dir_from_env` /
    38	  `spool_writer._state_dir` all honor it first), so this single anchor redirects
    39	  the whole audit/HMAC/spool surface.
    40	- **CLEARED** (so they default off `CEO_AUDIT_LOG_DIR`): `CEO_AUDIT_LOG_PATH`,
    41	  `CEO_AUDIT_LOG_ERR`, `CEO_AUDIT_LOG_LOCK`, `CEO_AUDIT_KEY_PATH`,
    42	  `CEO_AUDIT_LAST_HMAC_PATH`, `CEO_AUDIT_CHAIN_LENGTH_PATH`,
    43	  `CEO_AUDIT_LOG_FALLBACK_PATH`, `CEO_AUDIT_LOG_ROTATE_BYTES`,
    44	  `CEO_AUDIT_HMAC_DISABLE`.
    45	- **NOT touched:** `HOME` and `CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR`. `HOME` is only a *fallback*
    46	  for the audit dir — reached solely when `CEO_AUDIT_LOG_DIR` is unset, which the
    47	  fixtures always set. Redirecting `HOME` broke subprocesses that legitimately
    48	  need the real home for tooling (PyYAML in the macOS user-site, the GPG keyring,
    49	  npm/rsync) with zero isolation benefit; the function-scope assert plus the
    50	  byte-identity durable-fix proof cover the residual unset-fallback case.
    51	  `CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR` is not an audit-location carrier (no audit/HMAC/spool
    52	  resolver reads it), and redirecting it broke "the real repo's policy/config
    53	  files exist" tests. `CEO_AUDIT_SYNC_MODE` is left to `TestEnvContext`'s
    54	  per-test default (the session fixture must not force it, or the async-spool
    55	  opt-out tests would bypass the drain path they assert on).
    56	
    57	A redirected process **physically cannot** append to the live log. A
    58	function-scoped autouse assert (via the production resolver
    59	`audit_emit._audit_dir`, never a re-implementation) catches a test that mutates
    60	env back to the live dir mid-run.
    61	
    62	`TestEnvContext` continues to re-isolate **per test** on top of this; the
    63	session redirect makes the dir non-live up front so the per-test layer is purely
    64	additive (no test reds because the dir was "live at fixture time").
    65	
    66	For subprocess/multiprocessing tests, `TestEnvContext.subprocess_env()` (WS-C)
    67	builds the child env from the **same** carrier enumeration, so a spawned hook
    68	inherits the isolated destination — no second hand-maintained list to drift.
    69	
    70	### Axis 2 — write-time origin stamp (WS-D1)
    71	
    72	For the spool-drain path, the spool header is stamped `_origin: "test" | "live"`
    73	**at mint time** (the writer knows the truth; the drainer cannot infer it
    74	later). The drain (`spool_writer.drain_now`, the single orchestrator all three
    75	drain paths — opportunistic / atexit / signal — funnel through) quarantines
    76	`_origin:"test"` spool **only when the canonical destination is the live chain**
    77	(compared against `CEO_AUDIT_LIVE_LOG_PATH_SNAPSHOT`, captured before the
    78	redirect). A real session writes `_origin:"live"` and is never quarantined;
    79	legacy spool with no `_origin` defaults to `"live"` (fail-safe toward never
    80	losing a real event). If the snapshot is absent, the filter fails safe to
    81	**no quarantine**.
    82	
    83	### Import-time stale-copy closure (WS-D2)
    84	
    85	The recurring `unknown action 'output_scan_finding_suppressed'` breadcrumb is
    86	emitted only by a **stale pre-PLAN-106 `audit_emit.py`** loaded onto `sys.path`.
    87	WS-D2 extends the PLAN-118 import-time hard-raise to those archived + sandbox
    88	stale copies, so a stale `audit_emit` cannot be imported as `_lib.audit_emit`
    89	(while ACTIVE staging fixtures are carved out).
    90	
    91	## The escape hatch
    92	
    93	`@pytest.mark.allow_live_audit_dir` opts a single test out of the function-scope
    94	assert, for the rare test that genuinely exercises the real resolver. **Zero
    95	uses at ship.** A `validate-governance.sh` grep gate keeps it at zero; CODEOWNERS
    96	requires security-engineer review to add one. A reviewer adding the marker MUST
    97	confirm the test cannot instead use `TestEnvContext`.
    98	
    99	## Bash-probe orchestration protocol (load-bearing — the residual vector)
   100	
   101	The session fixture covers the **pytest** volume. It does **not** cover a bare
   102	Bash probe — a sub-agent (debate archetype, ad-hoc `pytest`/hook run) that the
   103	CEO spawns and that runs hooks in the **live shell** with the real `$HOME`,
   104	never entering a pytest session. No kernel guard can safely close this (a
   105	test-signal write-refusal is the rejected WS-B suppression vector). The mitigation
   106	is **orchestration discipline**, and it is mandatory:
   107	
   108	> **Any sub-agent the CEO spawns that may run `pytest`, invoke a hook, or
   109	> otherwise trigger an audit emit MUST run with the audit destination
   110	> redirected** — either by inheriting `CEO_TEST_HARNESS=1` **and** a scratch
   111	> `CEO_AUDIT_LOG_DIR` (e.g. `CEO_AUDIT_LOG_DIR=$(mktemp -d)`), or by running the
   112	> command under a `env -i`-style minimal environment that does not resolve the
   113	> live `~/.claude`.
   114	
   115	Concretely, before a probe that emits:
   116	
   117	```bash
   118	export CEO_TEST_HARNESS=1
   119	export CEO_AUDIT_LOG_DIR="$(mktemp -d)/audit"
   120	mkdir -p "$CEO_AUDIT_LOG_DIR"
   121	# ... run the pytest / hook / probe here ...
   122	```
   123	
   124	After any verification/probe activity in the live env, re-verify the chain
   125	**quiescently** (last thing, after all probe activity) before treating an
   126	`intact` read as authoritative:
   127	
   128	```bash
   129	python3 .claude/scripts/audit-verify-chain.py --strict-against-counter
   130	```
   131	
   132	## Triage: is a `tamper` read a real attack or test pollution?
   133	
   134	Per the S181 lesson, characterize by provenance **before** assuming a producer
   135	bug or rotating:
   136	
   137	- **Real `uuid` session_id + `null`/`CanonicalJsonError` HMAC** → a producer
   138	  float-in-HMAC bug (see the `cache_coverage_bps` fix, PLAN-118).
   139	- **Empty / `sess-N` / test session_id + non-null HMAC mismatch** → test-spool
   140	  pollution drained into the live chain. NOT a compromise; the durable fix is
   141	  this isolation harness.
   142	
   143	## See also
   144	
   145	- `.claude/hooks/_lib/test_isolation.py` — the shared isolation helper.
   146	- `.claude/hooks/_lib/testing.py` — `TestEnvContext` (per-test isolation +
   147	  `subprocess_env`).
   148	- `.claude/plans/PLAN-119-test-harness-audit-isolation.md` — the plan.
   149	- Lesson `feedback-verification-in-live-env-pollutes-audit-chain`.
