     1	"""S326 — collection-time audit isolation guard (anti-rot for a measured leak).
     2	
     3	pytest never runs fixtures under ``--collect-only``. The suite-wide audit-dir
     4	redirect (``_lib/test_isolation._ceo_audit_isolation_session``) is a session
     5	fixture, while the conftest's IMPORT-time work only pops
     6	``CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR_NATIVE``. So a test module that reaches an audit emitter
     7	at import time writes to the fallback ``$HOME/.claude/projects/<slug>`` — the
     8	LIVE HMAC chain — on every collect, and the whole-dir override carrier cannot
     9	redirect it (it was popped one step earlier).
    10	
    11	Measured 2026-08-24 (S326 boot): ``test_policy_mutations._POLICY_BASELINES``
    12	replayed the 82-row policy corpus at import → 124 signed, unattributable
    13	(``session_id=''``) events per ``pytest --collect-only``; ``verify-counts.sh``
    14	ran that collect before every commit → 19 runs / 2,356 links in 12 h = 79% of
    15	the live segment. The S321 cure (``9de4efc``) only ever covered fixture time.
    16	
    17	Two guards, ONE mechanism (a green negative is meaningful only because the
    18	positive control proves the detector can go red):
    19	
    20	- ``test_collecting_hook_legs_writes_no_audit_lines`` (always) and
    21	  ``test_collecting_all_testpaths_writes_no_audit_lines`` (where PyYAML is
    22	  importable; skips visibly elsewhere) — NEGATIVE, the class: collecting the
    23	  testpaths under a throwaway HOME (no audit carriers, no harness signals —
    24	  the exact shape ``verify-counts.sh`` runs in) writes ZERO audit-log lines
    25	  under that HOME.
    26	- ``test_positive_control_import_time_emitter_is_seen`` — the instrument: a
    27	  synthetic module that calls the policy engine at import, collected the same
    28	  way, DOES write lines under the throwaway HOME.
