   964	      # Step: User-template derivation gate (PLAN-169 wave-s330-F, ADR-197)
   965	      #
   966	      # `templates/settings/settings.user.json` is DERIVED from
   967	      # `settings.base.json` by the declared subtraction in its own
   968	      # `_derivation` key — never a hand-maintained second copy. That is
   969	      # the cure for the defect the wave measured: the old user template
   970	      # was a manual copy frozen at 9777a8d whose own `_comment` asserted
   971	      # a hook count and a byte-parity that nothing read, and both had
   972	      # rotted (26 basenames missing, a hand-narrowed matcher, a dropped
   973	      # second registration). A numeral in JSON prose is watched by
   974	      # nothing.
   975	      #
   976	      # `--check` re-derives the template from base + spec in memory and
   977	      # byte-diffs it against the committed file — the same
   978	      # regen-and-diff shape as the two idempotency steps above. The
   979	      # pytest suite already covers this (`.claude/scripts/tests/` IS
   980	      # collected by CI), so this step is not the only coverage; it
